    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the elite 82.97 efficiency rating of **Yordan Alvarez**. Facing George Klassen, **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a massive 6.12 xERA matchup and an elite 0.461 xwOBA projection, making him our primary engine for counting stats. Joining him at the top of the board are **Trea Turner** (72.38) and **Kyle Schwarber** (72.77), both of whom capitalize on high-leverage lineup spots and favorable platoon dynamics against Cade Gibson. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.06) remains a crucial start despite the lack of a defined SP, as he benefits from wind-out conditions and the optimization of his leadoff spot, which is essential for maintaining our aggressive stolen base strategy.\n\nThe decision-making process required tough calls, particularly regarding **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (67.94), whose heavy 16% park factor boost and 0.376 xwOBA allowed him to edge out more stable options. The most notable benching was **Chase Meidroth** (50.62); while his leadoff projection provided a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the high-upside ceiling of **Caleb Durbin** (67.40) against the vulnerable Merrill Kelly, noting that **Caleb Durbin** offers a more efficient path to SB accumulation. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Gary Sanchez** (40.68) and **Carson Benge** (53.71), as both face difficult matchups against Bryce Miller and Robbie Ray, respectively. With all lineups pending, we will monitor for any late scratches, but the current configuration maximizes our output while maintaining a sufficient buffer against the game-cap constraints inherent in our Ottoneu format.",
